course: dictionary
lesson: 3570
title: Festive and the feeling of a celebration
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you how people feel as well as what is happening. «At festive dinners even kids raise their juice and shout gānbēi! (cheers!)» Festive dinners are happy, celebrating dinners, and the shouting and raised glasses show the mood. Festive means happy and cheerful, like a party.
explain: The clues are the words around it. Dinner, raising glasses and shouting cheers all point to a celebration. Try swapping in your meaning: «At happy and cheerful dinners even kids raise their juice» still makes sense, so you have it right.
explain: Festive can also mean connected with a holiday or festival. «The festive season» means the holiday time, especially Christmas. The word links the mood to the occasion, so you can often spot it by asking: is this a party or a holiday?
fact: Festive means happy and cheerful, like a party or celebration.
fact: Festive can also mean connected with a holiday or festival, especially Christmas.
fact: «The festive season» means Christmas time in the UK, Ireland and Australia.
fact: «Festive decorations» are lights, streamers and tinsel that make a place look like a celebration.
fact: Festive is an adjective: it describes a noun, like a festive mood or festive food.
exercise: «At festive dinners even kids raise their juice and shout gānbēi!» What does festive mean here? | *Happy and celebrating | Quiet and serious | Late at night | Cold and empty
exercise: «The street was full of festive decorations.» What do the decorations suggest? | Sleepy and dark | Old and dusty | *Holiday cheer and celebration | Dirty and broken
exercise: Ella says «the festive season» is the time when people are at school all day. What is the festive season? | *Holiday time, especially Christmas | A school term | A time for tests | A rainy week in summer
test: «We ate festive food all afternoon, with music and laughter.» What does festive food suggest? | *Special food for a celebration | Plain and boring food for a normal day | Food eaten alone in silence | Food that has gone bad
test: Which holiday or festival can a festive season be connected with? | Monday mornings | A rainy walk | *Christmas | A school test
exam: Which word has the closest meaning to festive? | Tired | Gloomy | Empty | *Cheerful
